      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2010 The Authors. British Journal of Pharmacology © 2010 The British Pharmacological Society.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE",
            "content": "β\u2082-Adrenoceptor agonists are important therapeutic agents in the treatment of asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. The regular use of these drugs has been associated with proasthmatic-like changes that limit their efficacy and increase the risk of severe adverse reactions. We investigated whether the peroxisome-proliferator-activated receptor (PPAR)γ agonist rosiglitazone modulated salbutamol-induced β\u2082-adrenoceptor desensitization in vivo and in vitro."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "EXPERIMENTAL APPROACH",
            "content": "An in vivo model of homologous β\u2082-adrenoceptor desensitization, established in guinea-pigs by administering salbutamol continuously, was used to study the ability of rosiglitazone to prevent β\u2082-adrenoceptor tolerance. In vitro experiments on human bronchial smooth muscle cells were performed to increase the clinical relevance of the study."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "KEY RESULTS",
            "content": "In tracheal smooth muscle tissues from desensitized animals, we observed a decrease in the protective effect of salbutamol on carbachol-induced contraction, a hyperresponsiveness to cholinergic stimuli, a modest underexpression of β\u2082-adrenoceptor gene and a marked decrease in β-adrenoceptor number, relative to control values. Treatment with rosiglitazone preserved salbutamol relaxant activity, mitigated carbachol hyperresponsiveness and partially restored β\u2082-adrenoceptor binding sites in tracheal tissues from homologously desensitized animals. The highly selective PPARγ agonist, GW1929, reproduced the effect of rosiglitazone, in vivo. In vitro β\u2082-adrenoceptor desensitization decreased salbutamol-mediated cAMP production, without affecting forskolin responses and β\u2082-adrenoceptor expression. Rosiglitazone and 15-deoxy-Δ¹²(,)¹\u2074-prostaglandin J\u2082 restored salbutamol sensitivity in homologously desensitized cells."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS AND IMPLICATIONS",
            "content": "These data suggest a potential pharmacodynamic interaction between PPARγ agonists and salbutamol on airway smooth muscle responsiveness, supporting the therapeutic potential of this combination in chronic airway disease."
          }
        ]
      },
